# Generate an image from a text prompt and draw it with the pen.
#
# This tool calls an OpenAI-compatible ``/images/generations`` endpoint,
# writes the returned PNG into output_dir, and then feeds that PNG through
# the same tracing pipeline as image. It is disabled unless the skill
# config has imagegen_enabled=true and imagegen_base_url/imagegen_model are
# set; disabled or misconfigured calls return success=false without making
# any network request.
#
# The image is never downloaded from an arbitrary path: output_name is
# sanitised to a single .png filename inside output_dir, and the service URL
# comes from the skill config. The default trace mode for this tool is
# lineart (photos/grey artwork -> edge line art); skeleton or outline can be
# requested explicitly. dry_run=true still generates the image and plans the
# waypoints, but does not move the machine. Every successful generation
# writes the PNG into output_dir before any tracing happens.
#
# When this tool fails, fall back to scene with a simple declarative
# scene instead of retrying the same prompt.
#
# The prompt is sent verbatim plus imagegen_prompt_suffix when configured.
# Global motion parameters and pen heights remain owned by the primitive.
string  prompt
# Output PNG name inside output_dir. Empty -> timestamped name.
string  output_name
# Replace an existing output file.
bool    overwrite
# Tracing mode for the generated image: lineart, skeleton, outline, or
# empty/auto. Empty defaults to lineart for this tool.
string  trace
# Override the configured imagegen_size for this call (e.g. 1024x1024).
string  size
# Draw the generated image vertically mirrored (raw paper-raster direction).
# Default false draws it screen-upright; the written PNG is also tagged with
# robonix_orientation=screen so a later image call stays upright.
bool    flip
# Generate and plan only; do not move the machine.
bool    dry_run
# Run the primitive HOME routine after a successful draw.
bool    auto_home
# The pilot already homed before this call; do not repeat HOME.
bool    skip_home
plot/Workspace workspace
---
bool    success
string  message
# Absolute path of the generated PNG inside output_dir.
string  image_path
uint32  width_px
uint32  height_px
# Pen-up/down waypoints sent to the primitive.
uint32  points
float64 pixel_to_mm
bool    flip_y
string  trace
float64 min_x
float64 max_x
float64 min_y
float64 max_y
float64 elapsed_s